cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite the article below."
title: "Psi-treillis: divergence-free compression of periodic turbulent velocity fields, sampled on the GPU without rebuilding the grid"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pluenet
    given-names: Killian
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pluenet-Killian/Psi-treillis"
abstract: >-
  Psi-treillis compresses time sequences of incompressible, periodic velocity fields. The velocity is stored as the
  curl of a B-spline vector potential with integer coefficients, coded by temporal prediction and rANS, and decoded on
  the GPU. The decoded field is divergence-free by construction, it can be sampled at arbitrary points without
  rebuilding the grid, and a bound on the largest error is verified at compression. The repository holds the article,
  the codec, and the measurements behind every claim, including the claims its own measurements refute.
keywords:
  - lossy compression
  - turbulence
  - divergence-free
  - vector potential
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - scientific data
preferred-citation:
